UNIT hash_ok
KIND FUNCTIONAL
FIDELITY package
ANCHOR rederive@bb8ded84fa50 cli/verdict.mts hashOk (with hashHex, the digest it calls) — the code is the truth
ORACLE-CLASS deterministic
SIG hash_ok(text: text, want: text | none) -> bool
ENVELOPE text is well-formed Unicode text (any scalar values, NUL included, any length); want is none or any text.
  A want that is not a pin (R2) throws; nothing else throws inside this envelope. Lone surrogates, byte input, a
  missing want and non-text values of either argument are outside the abstract envelope (the js file widens to them).
DEPENDS-ON none
DESCRIPTION Does a pinned SHA-256 digest match the text? A pin is exactly 64 lowercase hexadecimal digits. The digest
  is SHA-256 (FIPS 180-4) over the UTF-8 encoding of the text, rendered as 64 lowercase hexadecimal digits. Only an
  absent pin (none) means "not pinned", and the answer is then true without looking at the text. Any other want must
  be a pin or the call throws; for a pin the answer is true exactly when the pin IS the digest rendering.
BEHAVIOR
R1 want is none -> true. Checked first: the text is not inspected, so its content never matters on this path.
R2 want is not a pin -> throws. A pin is text of exactly 64 characters, every one of them in 0-9 or a-f (lowercase
  ASCII only). So the empty text, any uppercase or mixed-case digit, a leading or trailing space or line break, 63 or
  65 characters, and any non-ASCII digit all throw. Checked before the text is inspected (R1, R2 hold whatever the text).
R3 Otherwise compute D = SHA-256 of the UTF-8 bytes of text, written as exactly 64 hexadecimal digits, lowercase,
  most significant byte first, two digits per byte with a leading zero kept. -> true iff want equals D exactly;
  any other pin -> false.
R4 The bytes are UTF-8 and only UTF-8: one to four bytes per scalar value, no byte-order mark added, none stripped (a
  leading U+FEFF is hashed as its three bytes), no terminator, no Unicode normalization (a composed and a decomposed
  spelling of the same word are different bytes, different digests). A digest of the UTF-16 code units or of a
  one-byte-per-character encoding of the same text does not match.
INVARIANT for every text t: hash_ok(t, none) = true, and hash_ok(t, D(t)) = true where D is R3's rendering; for
  every pin p other than D(t), hash_ok(t, p) = false.
ORACLE value -> oracles/hash_ok.json  CANONICAL-SHA256 98ff884cd54881436ae71b5613254a3bceede0ed4ba1a01ad1fd92108038661c
SCOPE IN: R1–R4 over well-formed text and a text-or-none pin. OUT (js extension only): lone surrogates, byte input,
  missing or non-text pins, non-text input. OUT entirely: the gate's own pin checks (rdv carried-data pinMatches, v05
  carried-table check), which inline different variants of this rule and do not call hashOk.
PROVENANCE rederive@bb8ded84fa50 (authority tree a2593d187a3b…), cli/verdict.mts lines 109–119: hashHex (node:crypto
  createHash('sha256') digest 'hex') and hashOk; driven through selfhost/seams/hash_ok.mjs as (text, want) -> hashOk(text, want).
